        "compile.py:14897-14900 vs 14840-14854 (MEDIUM): _tc_relevant_device_flags keep_macros has only 4 tile macros (SG_TUNED_TILE_M/_N/_DEC_DW_SPLITK/_VIT_DW_SPLITK), but _GEMM_TILE_DIM_NAMES routes 10 dims (incl. dec_gemm_stages, *_gemm_interleave, pipe_depth) to the real-TC timer. A config varying only one of those 6 extra dims pays a TC JIT build but the gemm-stages/interleave/pipe macros are stripped before the TC module is built, so the TC binary is byte-identical and the 'real TC' timing is just as blind to that dim as the cheap timer.",
