        "mma.cuh (CUTLASS Sm90 collective, where TMA/UTMALDG lives via op.initialize) is NOT included by any production code: zero non-third_party includers of sm_90/mma.cuh; only the closing-brace mma.cuh:871 references namespace sm90::mma; muon.h:9 mentions it in a comment only. By design (mma.cuh:14-18, host-launched, not device-callable, rejected for the megakernel).",
        "Production _dectc_codegen bake contains NO GemmUniversalAdapter/sm90_run_gemm/make_tma_copy/cp.async.bulk.tensor; the only 2 cuTensorMapEncode hits are CUDA driver header forward-decls (cuTensorMapEncodeTiled/Im2col), confirming the CUTLASS TMA path is unexercised by the megakernel.",
        "Descriptor bit-packing make_smem_desc (wgmma.cuh:219-241) verified: addr bits13:0, lbo>>4 bits29:16, sbo>>4 bits45:32, base_offset bits51:49, swizzle bits63:62 — NO field overlap; canonical builders make_desc_*_kmajor (wgmma.cuh:274-288) set lbo=MN*16, sbo=128 bytes matching cute Major::K.",
        "SwizzleMode enum (wgmma.cuh:167-172) = CUTLASS LayoutType (NONE=0/128B=1/64B=2/32B=3, non-size-ascending, earlier draft had 32B/128B swapped); correctness path ships kSwizzleNone (wgmma.cuh:157-165) and all production callers + selftest confirm kSwizzleNone.",
        "ss-wgmma issues wgmma_issue_n{8,16,32,64,96,128} (wgmma.cuh:442-561) hard-fix scaleA=scaleB=1 (literal '1, 1' in every asm); operand %-numbering verified correct for all six shapes; mainloop_kchain (wgmma.cuh:617-644) issues fixed-ascending k-order, k=0 ScaleD=0 overwrite then ScaleD=1 accumulate, fence/commit/wait_group<0> — bitwise-deterministic per DESIGN 3.1.",
        "mma.cuh shape-keyed operator cache (lines 156-367) keys on {M,N,K,A,B,C} because TMA tensor map encodes the global base address (lines 105-117 = load-bearing address-stability safety invariant); thread_local 16-slot direct-mapped, entry-owned workspace, mutex intentionally dropped. TF32 path flagged NOT bit-identical to scalar FP32 (lines 776-780).",
        "Fragment decode wgmma_frag_decode (wgmma.cuh:343-364): slab=i>>2, row=16*warp+(lane>>2)+8*(within>>1), col=(lane&3)*2+(within&1)+8*slab; single source of truth shared by epilogue store and gate reference (wgmma_selftest.cu:116-119)."
      ],
      "bugs": [
        "STALE/MISLEADING comment wgmma.cuh:416-421 claims 'canonical setting is TransA=0, TransB=1 ... B read transposed' but EVERY production caller and the selftest pass TransA=0,TransB=0 with both operands Major-K INTERLEAVE (tile_pipeline.cuh:335-339, model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh:759-760, model_stage_vit_tc.cuh:470-472, wgmma_selftest.cu:111). Not a code bug (function is parametric, prod passes 0,0) but doc could misdirect a future caller.",
        "Doc/impl drift wgmma.cuh:326-342 (frag-decode prose) sketches a 'group_of_8=i/8' factoring with an unfinished '+ ...' that does not match the implemented slab=i>>2 form at wgmma.cuh:343-364. Implemented form is authoritative/gate-validated; comment is incomplete (cosmetic).",
        "Latent: make_smem_desc addr field (wgmma.cuh:226,231) is (byte&0x3FFFF)>>4 OR'd at bit0 with no explicit &0x3FFF mask; safe for H100 (max 14528 < 0x3FFF for 227KB smem, verified) but would collide into reserved bits 14:15 if a future arch had >256KB smem-per-block. Not currently a bug."
      ],
      "dead_code": [
        "mma.cuh sm90_get_workspace (lines 68-81) is defined but unused by the only present code paths (the cache uses entry-OWNED workspaces, lines 274-282, and the 1x1x1 kGemm path reports workspace size 0 per lines 119-127). Within-file unused helper. NOTE: mma.cuh as a whole is unwired into the megakernel BY DESIGN (host-launched CUTLASS for Muon/SG2 behind -DWITH_CUTLASS, mma.cuh:13-18) — NOT classified as dead code, only its TMA/UTMALDG path is unexercised by the production L3-TC path."
      ],
      "digest_path": "/workspace/phase0c/wgmma_mma_substrate.md"
