      "top_findings": [
        "All 9 .so are sm_90a persistent megakernels (sg::fused::sm90::fused_{decoder,mamba,vit}_megakernel_tc<OptId> + sg2_meta_optimizer_megakernel); GMMA==HGMMA only, two shapes: HGMMA.64x128x16.F32.BF16 (BF16->F32 main wgmma) + HGMMA.64x8x16.F16. Per file (HGMMA/LDGSTS): gopt _ops 1415/412, nvcc_fastmath 1340/352, task11 A/B/C all 45/32, tune_base 1822/352, tune_2944 2542/0, tune_7a88 3078/352, tune_aba7 2770/0.",
        "ZERO UTMALDG (TMA) in all 9 binaries despite -DCUDA_TMA_ENABLED=1; staging is cp.async (LDGSTS) or direct. SG_TUNED_TMA=0 in every hashed config.",
        "Shipped grokking_optimizers/_ops.so per-model: decoder 590 HGMMA + 412 LDGSTS, vit 825 HGMMA/0 LDGSTS, mamba 0 HGMMA/0 LDGSTS (mamba NOT tensor-core in shipped build), sg2_meta 0; production _ops (#1) and tune_base (#6) are DIFFERENT cubins (HGMMA 1415 vs 1822, decoder SHARED 26384 vs 44212) — shipped uses baked levers, tune_base has no SG_TUNED.",
        "The 4 tune11 hashes: BASE has NO SG_TUNED defines (=primary_artifact, tuned_config:null); 2944=Optuna trial3 (block832/unroll128/maxrreg176/cluster1,1,4/tileN64/async4/stages1, 15.13ms), 7a88=trial5 (block896/maxrreg128/cluster2,1,1/tileN128/stages2, 17.84ms), aba7=trial7 (block352/unroll8/maxrreg116/cluster4,2,1/splitK4, 14.71ms best) — full lever matrix in digest.",
        "ALL 3 hashed tune candidates FAILED parity gate: trials 3/5/7 numerical_status=numerical_fail; compile cache keeps tuned_config:null + BASE as primary -> none promotable to production (HARD gate held). tune11_out/.compile_cache.json variant_artifacts maps config_key->hash dir (block352/maxrreg116->aba7, block896/maxrreg128->7a88, block832/maxrreg176->2944).",
        "Observable lever->SASS effects: SG_TUNED_TILE_N=64 (2944) -> main wgmma HGMMA.64x64x16 (vs 64x128x16 in base/aba7); maxrregcount honored ONLY for 2944 (REG:175), infeasible/raised to 255 for 7a88(cap128)/aba7(cap116); SHARED budget tracks levers 2944~34KB<aba7~40KB<base~44KB<7a88~48KB; LDGSTS present(352) base/7a88 vs elided(0) 2944/aba7.",
        "task11 A_sk4/B_sk4/C_sk2 all from mega_decoder_real_adamw_tc.cu, SG_DEC_SCALAR_MEGAKERNEL=0 (persistent, not scalar), OptId0 only, identical 45 HGMMA/32 LDGSTS. A=vanilla nvcc, B=compile.py augmented flags (same defines as A, +0.43% noise), C=B with DEC_DW_SPLITK=2 vs 4 (autotuner pick, -2.09% vs B at 492ms/20.1TF/s). B vs C cubins NOT byte-identical (split-K changes DW reduction loop, not GEMM count).",
        "task11 perf (.task11_perf_authoritative.log) ~500ms / ~2% roofline = slow nvcc/bench baselines, NOT production persistent-megakernel throughput. All decoder kernels REG:255 (launch-bound), LOCAL:0 (no local spills), STACK is launch-bounds frame. cub::EmptyKernel present in every cubin (CUB device-scan dep)."
      ],
      "bugs": [
        "Mamba codegen divergence: shipped grokking_optimizers/_ops.so mamba megakernel emits 0 HGMMA, but all tune11 builds emit 482-872 HGMMA for mamba (tune11_out/.../mega_mamba_real_adamw_tc_launcher.cu) — the baked-lever production path gates the mamba GEMM off tensor cores while tune dirs route it through wgmma; confirm which is intended (not a crash, a real shipped-vs-tune divergence of 'the same' kernel).",
        "7a882d5329a20564 (maxrregcount=128) and aba71f216d321649 (maxrregcount=116) register caps are infeasible: ptxas silently emits REG:255 ignoring the cap (build.ninja line 7 --maxrregcount); the autotuner recorded these as numerical_fail (trials_adamw_decoder_sm_90a.jsonl trial 5/7), so the cap never took effect."
      ],
