      ],
      "top_findings": [
        "All 5 variants share ONE kernel sg::fused::sm90::fused_decoder_megakernel_tc<OptId=0>; HGMMA=50, wgmma.arrive=50, LDGSTS=36, DEPBAR=86, REG=255, STACK=800 are IDENTICAL across baseline/deep_s3/deep_s3_ptx/deep_s4/postedit — the upgrades change NONE of the tensor-core program, only smem placement + ring depth (cuobjdump -sass/-res-usage on extracted cubins).",
        "baseline.cubin md5==postedit.cubin md5 (67922b84, 306936B) AND address-stripped SASS diff is EMPTY AND PTX md5s match (7ee1d75f/d3fecaa2) -> postedit_default is a strict NO-OP vs baseline (identity post-edit / control).",
        "deep_s3.cubin md5==deep_s3_ptx.cubin md5 (1c979e89, 312376B) AND address-stripped SASS diff EMPTY -> the nvcc-compiled deep-ring path and the hand-PTX-edited path converge to byte-identical machine code (PTX-edit toolchain is faithful).",
        "The deep upgrade = static->dynamic smem: baseline PTX has demoted '.shared .align 16 ...E2sm[18064]' (baseline ptx:75); deep_s3_ptx replaces it with '.extern .shared .align 16 .b8 _ZN2sg5fused4sm9013sg_dectc_poolE[]' (deep_s3_ptx ptx:43) matching header fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:688-689; static SHARED drops 44436->26384 (the 18064B DecTcSmem moved to DYNAMIC smem).",
        "Every baseline 'E2sm+X' smem ref becomes 'sg_dectc_pool+(X+8192)' in deep_s3_ptx (16384->24576, 17408->25600, ...): exact +8192B pool-base shift, 1:1 across all 36+ offsets; rest of the 14.5k-line PTX diff is pure register renumbering induced by this single structural change.",
        "Deep path measurably reduces synchronization: BAR.SYNC 143->134 (-9) and FENCE 18->9 (-9) on deep_s3/deep_s3_ptx/deep_s4 — the single-arena dynamic pool removes redundant cross-region fences/barriers the static multi-array layout needed (cuobjdump -sass counts).",
        "deep_s4 = deep_s3 + ONE extra ring stage (S=4 vs S=3): max smem offset 0x6650->0x8650 (+0x2000=+8192B = 1 ring slot sA4KB+sB4KB at TILE_N=128/IL=2); ring-index arithmetic flips from 30x 'IMAD ...0x3' (mul-by-3, depth 3 non-pow2) to 3x (depth-4 uses cheap &3 mask), so deep_s4 has FEWER instrs (18240 vs 18480) despite deeper ring.",
        "Verified probe binaries on CPU: ./sizeprobe gives sizeof(DecTcSmem)=18064(S2)/26256(S3)/34448(S4) at TILE_M=128 (18064 exactly matches baseline E2sm[18064]); probe.cu static_asserts sizeof==50832 at TILE_M=256/IL=4/S=4 (the only >48KB legal config the gate routes to dynamic); ./grid confirms only TILE_N=256 IL>=2 S=4 (49.64KB) busts the 48KB static cap. Gate = SG_DEC_TC_DYNAMIC_SMEM = PIPE && (STAGES>2) at fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:464."
      ],
      "bugs": [],
      "dead_code": [
