      "top_findings": [
        "SHARD SCOPE: all 25 files are the FOUNDATIONAL L3-TC build-out era (June 9-12 2026, CLI v2.1.169-173). The UPGRADED L3-TC baked levers (SG_TUNED_DEC_FWD_PIPE/FWD_STAGES/DW_STAGE/P1_SUBTILE_S, _dectc_codegen) are ABSENT from this shard (raw grep = 0 hits); the 1.49/2.05/4.02 hits here are false-positives (grad rel-errors, not the lever speedups). Those levers are from a later session outside shard 2.",
        "AUTOTUNER->SHIPPED-.so LINKAGE GAP (agent a2b9257f): kernels consume SG_TUNED_BLOCK_SIZE via #ifndef-default-256 + __launch_bounds__, but setup.py never emits -DSG_TUNED_BLOCK_SIZE -> the block-size dim (and most tuned dims) is DECORATIVE for the shipped _ops.so. A dim is swept-live (JIT sees -D via resolve_macros compile.py:2707) but only SHIPPED-live if its key is in _tuned_inject.py::MACROS (currently only 5 phase-1 keys). cluster_shape and the R2 wgmma.cuh/tile_pipeline.cuh macros are confirmed decorative.",
        "SG_TUNED_* REGISTRATION = 6-spot recipe (agent a622b85e): _sm90/_gfx942_full_space _dim() + auto _DEAD_KEY_DIMS + megakernel_cell_search_space + _COST_MODEL_CANONICAL_DIM_VALUES(4515) + _LIVE_TUNING_DIMS(1263) + _tuned_inject.py(MACROS/_EMIT_ORDER/_PERSIST_KEYS, the ship gate). Liveness auto-derived: _kernel_source_macros (compile.py:1277) greps for SG_TUNED_ token; registering a token NOT in source is worse than no-op (_pin_dead_dims:1393 drops it). Owner rule #9: all perf tuning -> compile.py, hand-tuning banned.",
        "ROOFLINE NUMBERS (quiet GPU, B=16384): mamba TC megakernel adamw/lion/grokfast = 1.452/1.449/1.435 TF/s = 0.59% roof, wall ~135ms; '0.46x' = TC was 0.46x scalar speed (only 4 projections TC, selective scan stays scalar register-resident = bottleneck). Decoder megakernel is OCCUPANCY-PINNED at 1 CTA/SM: saturates B~2k, declines past 16k -> batch does NOT buy roofline fraction; path forward = multi-CTA-per-tensor tiling. Final 33/33 AFTER table: mean roof% 1.150, median 1.293 (vs 0.48-0.49% before).",
        "MAMBA-LANE 0.46x->2.145x FLIP (agent add6cd61): forced bf16-wgmma TC wall 113.768ms vs scalar 244.035ms = 2.145x TC WINS, via 2 grad-assembly fixes (mbtc_partial_reduce by-tensor->flat-element striping using all 132 CTAs; mbtc_dw_biases single-owner striping, ~19% gain 139.9->113.2ms). 0.170% of bf16-TC peak is STRUCTURAL (scan-bound, projections saturated). occ=2 (__launch_bounds__(256,2)) measured 1.14x faster but REVERTED -- breaks A/A/A determinism (max|d|=2.3e-10 vs bit-identical); GridBarrier is 1-CTA/SM by design.",
        "33/33 L3-TC COMPLETION + 4 WON'T-GROK cells: final 3 mamba SG cells (SG11/SG15/SG2) landed A/A/A bit-deterministic (agent accfdf30, commits 4dcb7ee+379c746); race-fix 0b57f7e covered the SAM double-forward + SG2 segmented-sort. Documented WON'T-GROK (not bugs): SG11 (train 0.998@step400 then collapse 0.014), SG15 (memorize-then-collapse, inherent meta-net dynamics), SG2 (CSA indexer drops idx_UQ + /sqrt(rank=4) not /sqrt(d=8), diverges N>64), neuralgrok-on-L3 (frozen amplifier). EXPECTED grok = other 8/11.",
        "PER-KERNEL LATENT BUGS (June 9 audits): supergrok15_sm90.cuh hardcodes SG15_H=64 vs default hidden_dim=32 -> OOB reads/corrupt mu (HIGH; later FIXED in commit 94a0b2e 64->32); grokadamw_sm90.cuh Q3 path block_size floor-div -> OOB read of ea_scales when N%num_scales!=0 (HIGH, reachable via grokadamw_step_q3); attention_sm90.cuh softmax_lse wrong dtype (expects fp32, binding passes as ActT) -> silent corruption under bf16.",
        "VERIFICATION-GAUNTLET PLAN + 4 OPEN AUDIT FINDINGS (main session 80b51e31): (a) vaporware multistep gates referenced but never defined in test_l3tc_tail_gate.py:303-339 [later AUTHORED as test_multistep_parity.py, GPU-run green commit 3555ff9]; (b) check_math_single_source.py:377 apply-call check is WARN-only (has TODO harden-to-fail); (c) ci.yml:1316 runs 'pytest -m not hw' -> HW gate excluded from CI (all runners CPU-only); (d) SG2/vit test-state-leakage (per-op oracle perturbs device-global -> NaN; needs subprocess-per-cell isolation). profile_maximal audits SASS not PTX; WGMMA shows as HGMMA (grep wgmma=0 is false-neg)."
