      "top_findings": [
        "ERA: this shard (dated 2026-06-09..06-12) PREDATES the upgraded-L3-TC baked levers — zero hits for FWD_PIPE/FWD_STAGES/DW_STAGE/P1_SUBTILE_S/_dectc_codegen across all 24 files; the 1.49/4.02/2.05 grep matches are coincidental profiler/UUID fragments, not lever speedups. It documents the substrate the levers were later built on.",
        "wgmma race-path wired (agent-ae6f9cfa): new launcher TUs mega_{decoder,vit}_real_adamw_tc_launcher.cu + gemm_impl_for_cell; KEY PERF FACT = at grok sizes bf16 TC is SLOWER than eager-adamw (decoder ~0.57x, vit ~0.17x) and only mamba scalar-L3 beats eager (~1.8x); all 33 roofline rows <3% of roofline (latency-bound). No commit.",
        "OWNER BASELINE 'all 33 cells L3-TC' was NOT reached (agent-a87939bd): 4/33 converted (adamw+lion x{decoder,vit} wgmma, adamw/mamba scalar), 29 blocked each cited. Premise overturned: grokfast/grokadamw/neuralgrok are NOT 'nothing-needed' (state-aware gate catches grokfast ema cold-start rel 0.98). lion is the only genuinely-direct new convert.",
        "Committed perf win c67cb66 (agent-a228af2): embedding-grad assembly O(V.d.T)->O(d.T) via counting-sort + single-owner bias-reduce; d=128 production 105.8->35.4 ms (3.0x), grad_asm 80.6->8.0 ms; A/A/A bit-identical, wiring 33/33, test_decoder_tc 18/18.",
        "sm_90 autotuner 3-defect fix committed 84db23f (agent-ac596b81): (1) GEMM-BLIND winner-timer fixed (was timing opt.step() on dummy param via surrogate TU; now _time_megakernel_tc_step builds real-TC TU with tuned macros at compile.py:13179/13673), (2) added tile_m/tile_n/{dec,vit,mb}_dw_splitk dims -> SG_TUNED_* macros, (3) per-model tuned schema. This is the producer of the SG_TUNED_* macros the later baked levers extend.",
        "wgmma substrate had 3 correctness bugs fixed (agent-a4ee747): wrong CUTLASS K-major smem layout + descriptor LBO/SBO + TransB=1 (should be 0, gave A=I max_err 1.178); pipeline deadlock from elect_one_sync electing per-warp leader on init(1) barriers (fixed init(128)+all-128-arrive); 18/18 gates pass, no commit.",
        "Committed cells: looksam/vit GREEN fb997a9 (4.194 TF/s, A/A/A bit-identical); looksam/mamba land-dormant-BLOCKED 3725472; mamba muon 6cd6ce1 (25->26/33). Wave-2 vit (wf_694d43eb): muon/vit GREEN 4.06 + grokadamw/vit GREEN 5.69 via append-only aux_lr/aux_beta1/aux_beta2 FusedScalars widening; prodigy/vit REGRESSED (A/A/A NaN, not green).",
        "Mechanism-DROP audit (agent-a06072956): SG2 is the exemplar — lamb (void)-discarded at supergrok2_sm90.cuh:1805/1885 + mu buffer repurposed (slow-grad EMA ref vs expert-output EMA kernel); SG11 lamb dead-in-both vs SG15 lamb live (bindings.cpp:1358 vs :1486). All other 8 optimizers EQUIVALENT. parity infra is transcribed from kernels so cannot catch this class."
      ],
      "bugs": [
        "Muon L1 standalone inverted weight-decay: muon_sm90.cuh:256-258 computed p*(1-decay_factor) instead of canonical muon.h:71-72 p*decay_factor; retained ~2% of weights/step. FIXED in bringup session (agent-acb0479f / main e69607ce) -> Muon went flat-at-random to grokking at 600 steps. Verify shipped tree has the fix.",
        "SG2 lamb dropped + mu repurposed: supergrok2_sm90.cuh:1805,:1885 '(void)lamb_eff'; kernel runs g+alpha*mu_new with mu=expert-output EMA, while reference (supergrok2.py:2362-2364) is smart_grad + lamb_eff*(slow-grad EMA) -> race executes a different algorithm. Orthogonal GRU/sort fix (agent-ac35e460) addressed an 85%-wrong expert output but not the lamb-drop.",
